implementationPlan.description:
The four DEFAULT-RUN drives. Each one takes its approval from the preview instead of building it by hand.
- deploy-environment.spec.ts:90-106 (`landAndPublish`)
- deploy-fake-docker.spec.ts:~100-115
- deploy-migrations.spec.ts:~133-148
- lane-rollback-incident.ts:~175-190, which deploy-rollback-incident.spec.ts uses

In each drive:
- call `readPublicationApproval(lane, goalId, REMOTE_URL)` after the landing;
- assert `approval.sha` equals the landed sha and `approval.remoteUrl` equals REMOTE_URL. This proves the preview names the commit this drive just landed, which is a stronger check than the old hand-built value;
- pass that approval to the existing `repository.publish` dispatch unchanged, still expecting ACCEPTED;
- delete the now-dead `branch: "main"` literal and the hand-built `repositoryId`;
- remove any import or local that no longer has a use (`publicationRepositoryId`, the identity resolution), and nothing else. Keep a local if another part of the file still reads it.
The file-local `command` helpers stay as they are: they are hand-mirrored on purpose.
Run `pnpm exec tsc -p tests/e2e/control-room/tsconfig.json`; it must exit 0.
